# CASM Phase 12 WP70 trusted reference: casmrelacc
#
# Independently hand-assembled from the casmrelacc fixture source in
# cmake/GenerateCasmTestFixtures.cmake. NOT produced by CASM. Proves the
# "accepted" side of WP64's representability contract -- a relocatable
# label combined with a static addend via '+', with the static side
# wrapped in an explicit parenthesized group -- through the real R6
# relocation table, for the first time reached via WP67's recursive
# parsePrimary/parseOperatorTail architecture rather than the old flat
# single-addend evaluator every pre-Phase-12 R6-verified fixture
# (casmrelop1/casmrelop2/casmreloc1) used exclusively. No existing
# fixture anywhere combines a relocatable label with an addend AND
# verifies the resulting R6 table -- confirmed by reading every one of
# them (WP70 plan's own Research Findings).
#
# Source (no .ORG -- default relocatable output, base $3400):
#   - START: JMP MID
#   - MID: LDA TARGET+(1+0)
#   - TARGET: NOP
#
# START = $3400. JMP MID is 3 bytes ($3400-$3402, absolute, MID's own
# address is not yet known at this point but resolves to $3403). MID =
# $3403. LDA TARGET+(1+0) is 3 bytes ($3403-$3405, absolute -- TARGET is
# symbol-derived so FORCE_ABS applies regardless of value): the '+'
# combines relocatable TARGET with the static group (1+0)=1, accepted
# per WP64's rule (one relocatable + one static). TARGET = $3406
# (immediately after this instruction). TARGET+(1+0) = $3406+1 = $3407.
# The NOP defining TARGET ($EA) is at $3406.
#
# MID is itself a label in this same relocatable assembly, so JMP MID is
# ALSO a relocatable reference in its own right (easy to miss when
# focused on TARGET as "the" test subject -- caught by the real COMP
# mismatch below, not assumed correct from the design alone) -- the same
# "JMP LABEL, absolute, high byte relocatable" pattern casmrelop1.ref.hex
# already established at its own offset 2.
#
# Hand assembly:
#   00 34        PRG load-address header ($3400, little-endian)
#   4C 03 34     JMP $3403                    (MID)
#   AD 07 34     LDA $3407                    (TARGET+(1+0) = $3406+1)
#   EA           NOP                          (at $3406, defines TARGET)
#   02 00        R6 table entry: offset 2 (JMP MID's high byte)
#   05 00        R6 table entry: offset 5 (LDA's high byte) -- only the
#                high byte of a page-relocated absolute address ever
#                needs patching, matching casmrelop1's own established
#                pattern
#   00 34        R6 footer: base address ($3400, little-endian)
#   02 00        R6 footer: relocation entry count (2)
#   52 36        R6 footer: ASCII magic "R6"
#
# bytes: 19
# sha256: ddc2d61d50544ce458be4f3e85f27f5ca3224f8d3d2aac94a90132b285d22889
# source_sha256: casmrelacc.seq=c2e1660da6a0f301de5dff80827f7d4ef8d267b4e8a5af49387b12421cc47471

00 34
4C 03 34
AD 07 34
EA
02 00
05 00
00 34
02 00
52 36
